      "short": "Correct answer: B.",
      "worked": "There are $60\\times24\\times365$ minutes in one year, and $1000$ mL in one litre.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4\\div1000\\text{ L}}{1\\div60\\div24\\div365\\text{ year}}&=\\frac{4\\times60\\times24\\times365}{1\\times1000}\\text{ L/year}\\\\\\frac{4\\div1000\\text{ L}}{1\\div60\\div24\\div365\\text{ year}}&=\\frac{4\\times60\\times24\\times365}{1000}\\text{ L/year}\\end{align*}$$\nCorrect answer: B.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
